    {
      "reference": "arXiv:1104.2661 (Int.J.Mod.Phys.A 26 (2557), 2011)",
      "authors": "Valtancoli, Paolo",
      "description": "One-loop scalar box integral I^m(s,t,m) with one external mass (p1^2 = m^2, other legs on-shell massless) and massless internal lines, in d=4-2*eps. Symanzik polynomial F = x1*x3*(-s) + x2*x4*(-t) + x1*x4*(-m^2) (Eq. 4.1). Solved exactly via Feynman parameters as a sum of three 2F1 hypergeometric functions in arguments (s+t-m^2)/t, (s+t-m^2)/s, m^2(s+t-m^2)/(s*t) (Eqs. 4.7-4.9). Reduces to the massless box in the limit m^2 -> 0. Also reproduced via a two-fold Mellin-Barnes representation in Section 5 (Eq. 5.2), with the F_2 Appell function reduced to a single-variable 2F1 via the Bailey identity (Eq. 5.15) and spurious terms cancelling among I^m_1, I^m_{2a}, I^m_{2b} (Eq. 5.20).",
